Here is the step-by-step solution to determine when and where the second train catches up with the first.

### Step 1: Determine the head start of the first train

First, we calculate how much time the first train has been traveling before the second train departs.

*   First train departure time: 3:15 pm
*   Second train departure time: 4:00 pm
*   Time difference: 45 minutes

Convert this time into hours, as the speed is given in km/h:
$$ 45 \text{ minutes} = \frac{45}{60} \text{ hours} = 0.75 \text{ hours} $$

### Step 2: Calculate the distance the first train has traveled

Now, we calculate the distance the first train covers during its 0.75-hour head start.

*   Speed of first train ($v_1$): 80 km/h
*   Time ($t_{headstart}$): 0.75 hours

$$ \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} $$
$$ d_{headstart} = 80 \text{ km/h}
